   "source": [
    "# Eumon processor executed with Insula OGC API\n",
    "\n",
    "## Overview\n",
    "This notebook runs a processing job using the *Eumon* processor on the **Insula** platform through its\n",
    "**OGC API – Processes** interface, then retrieves and downloads the results.\n",
    "\n",
    "It authenticates with an **API key**, submits an execution request to a\n",
    "specific process (process `251`, the *Eumon* processor) for a given\n",
    "Sentinel-3 product, polls the job status, and finally downloads the output\n",
    "files (GeoTIFFs) produced by the job.\n",
    "**To execute it on Insula Experiment:** log-in to https://code.insula.earth/\n",
    "in the upper tabs click on 'File' and then on 'Open from URL', and paste in the window that opens the raw link to this notebook: \n",
    "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cgi-italy/earthcode-notebooks/refs/heads/master/EuMonExperiment.ipynb"
    "\n",
    "***Steps***:\n",
    "1. **Configure** – set the base URL, the Sentinel-3 product identifier, the\n",
    "   area of interest (AOI), and the processing date.\n",
    "2. **Submit the job** – POST the inputs to the process execution endpoint and\n",
    "   receive a job ID.\n",
    "3. **Check status** – query the job endpoint to see whether it is still\n",
    "   running, succeeded, or failed.\n",
    "4. **Retrieve & download results** – fetch the list of output files and\n",
    "   download each one locally."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "50dfbaa6-832a-4d72-8c95-a3e4f10cd72f",
   "metadata": {
    "editable": true,
    "slideshow": {
     "slide_type": ""
    },
    "tags": []
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import requests\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import getpass\n",
    "import json\n",
    "import re"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "19027b07-d28b-4631-86f8-4967653b3edf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Authentication\n",
    "Prompt for the Insula API key. \n",
    "You can generate an API key here: [Generate an API key](https://insula.earth/awareness/account/api_keys)\n",
    "\n",
    "`getpass` hides the input so the key is not\n",
    "stored in plain text in the notebook. The key is reused in the request\n",
    "headers of every subsequent call."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "id": "45a70d3a-cf2a-4897-869f-37e401b525d6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdin",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      " ········\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "API_KEY=getpass.getpass()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "09ed6216-1663-4a4b-a962-2ec42953ef4c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Configuration\n",
    "Define the parameters for this run:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `sentinel_file_identifier` – the Sentinel-3 product to process. You can browse the Sentinel-3 catalogue at [Browse Insula Catalogue](https://insula.earth/perception/discovery/platform_catalogue) by selecting CATALOGUE=\"Open Data\" and COLLECTION=\"Sentinel-3\"\n",
    "- `sentinel_search_link` – the catalogue search URL that points to that\n",
    "  product; it is passed to the processor as the `SENTINEL3` input.\n",
    "- `aoi` – the area-of-interest identifier. 1=Tanzania, 2=Albania, 3=Italy\n",
    "- `processingDate` – the product date of the chosen Sentinel-3 product. When browsing the catalogue it is shown right under the product identifier."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "id": "2e6b06a9-7263-4079-a0d3-38c589a1e05c",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "BASE_URL=\"https://insula.earth\"\n",
    "\n",
    "sentinel_file_identifier=\"S3A_OL_2_WFR____20180211T062446_20180211T062746_20210721T031427_0179_027_362______MAR_R_NT_003.SEN3\"\n",
    "sentinel_search_link = (\n",
    "    \"https://insula.earth/secure/api/v2.0/search\"\n",
    "    \"?page=0&resultsPerPage=20&catalogue=SATELLITE&mission=sentinel3\"\n",
    "    f\"&identifier={sentinel_file_identifier}\"\n",
    "    f\"&identifier={sentinel_file_identifier}\"\n",
    ")\n",
    "aoi=\"1\"\n",
    "processingDate=\"2018-02-11T00:00:00.000Z\""
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "4989acee-f6c4-4352-b2cd-790c8846850d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Submit the processing job\n",
    "Build the execution request and POST it to the process `251` execution\n",
    "endpoint. The body follows the OGC API – Processes format, wrapping each\n",
    "input value in a list under the `inputs` object.\n",
    "\n",
    "The response contains the created job, including its `id`, which is used in\n",
    "the following cells."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "id": "4122d7f3-c410-403a-a1c6-bdf905104947",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "url = BASE_URL + \"/ogcapi/processes/251/execution\"\n",
    "HEADERS = {\n",
    "    'Authorization': f'Apikey {API_KEY}',\n",
    "    'Content-Type': 'application/json'\n",
    "}\n",
    "inputs_json={\n",
    "    \"inputs\": {\n",
    "        \"SENTINEL3\": [sentinel_search_link],\n",
    "        \"AOI\": [aoi],\n",
    "        \"PROCESSING_DATE\": [processingDate]\n",
    "    }\n",
    "}\n",
    "run_request=requests.post(url,headers=HEADERS, data=json.dumps(inputs_json), verify=True)\n",
    "run_request_dict = json.loads(run_request.text)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "id": "87669853-480f-4677-85d3-e60cce9bc1af",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "{'title': None,\n",
       " 'description': None,\n",
       " 'keywords': [],\n",
